      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "Given that the line $y = ax + b$ passes through the points $(4,5)$ and $(8,17)$, we can use the coordinates of these points to set up a system of linear equations to solve for $a$ and $b$.\n\nFirst, substitute the point $(4,5)$ into the equation $y = ax + b$:\n\\[5 = 4a + b \\quad \\text{(Equation 1)}\\]\n\nNext, substitute the point $(8,17)$ into the equation $y = ax + b$:\n\\[17 = 8a + b \\quad \\text{(Equation 2)}\\]\n\nNow we have a system of linear equations:\n\\[\n\\begin{cases}\n5 = 4a + b & \\text{(Equation 1)} \\\\\n17 = 8a + b & \\text{(Equation 2)}\n\\end{cases}\n\\]\n\nTo solve for $a$ and $b$, we can subtract Equation 1 from Equation 2 to eliminate $b$:\n\\[\n17 - 5 = 8a + b - (4a + b) \\\\\n12 = 4a \\\\\na = 3\n\\]\n\nNow that we have $a = 3$, we can substitute this value back into Equation 1 to solve for $b$:\n\\[\n5 = 4(3) + b \\\\\n5 = 12 + b \\\\\nb = 5 - 12 \\\\\nb = -7\n\\]\n\nThus, we have $a = 3$ and $b = -7$. To find $a - b$, we simply subtract $b$ from $a$:\n\\[\na - b = 3 - (-7) = 3 + 7 = 10\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is $\\boxed{10}$.",
