      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To solve for \\(a - b\\) given that the line \\(y = ax + b\\) passes through the points \\((4,5)\\) and \\((8,17)\\), we can follow these steps:\n\n1. **Substitute the points into the equation \\(y = ax + b\\):**\n\n   For the point \\((4,5)\\):\n   \\[\n   5 = 4a + b\n   \\]\n\n   For the point \\((8,17)\\):\n   \\[\n   17 = 8a + b\n   \\]\n\n2. **Set up a system of linear equations:**\n\n   We have:\n   \\[\n   4a + b = 5 \\quad \\text{(Equation 1)}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   8a + b = 17 \\quad \\text{(Equation 2)}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Eliminate \\(b\\) by subtracting Equation 1 from Equation 2:**\n\n   \\[\n   (8a + b) - (4a + b) = 17 - 5\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   8a + b - 4a - b = 12\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   4a = 12\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   a = 3\n   \\]\n\n4. **Substitute \\(a = 3\\) back into Equation 1 to solve for \\(b\\):**\n\n   \\[\n   4(3) + b = 5\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   12 + b = 5\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   b = 5 - 12\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   b = -7\n   \\]\n\n5. **Calculate \\(a - b\\):**\n\n   \\[\n   a - b = 3 - (-7) = 3 + 7 = 10\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\(a - b\\) is \\(\\boxed{10}\\).",
