      "text": "Given the points $(4,5)$ and $(8,17)$, we can use the equation of a line $y = ax + b$. Substituting the given points into the equation, we get two equations:\n\n1. For the point $(4,5)$:\n\\[5 = 4a + b \\quad \\text{(Equation 1)}\\]\n\n2. For the point $(8,17)$:\n\\[17 = 8a + b \\quad \\text{(Equation 2)}\\]\n\nWe now have a system of linear equations:\n\\[\n\\begin{cases}\n5 = 4a + b \\\\\n17 = 8a + b\n\\end{cases}\n\\]\n\nTo eliminate $b$, subtract Equation 1 from Equation 2:\n\\[\n17 - 5 = 8a + b - (4a + b)\n\\]\n\\[\n12 = 4a\n\\]\n\\[\na = 3\n\\]\n\nNow substitute $a = 3$ back into Equation 1 to find $b$:\n\\[\n5 = 4(3) + b\n\\]\n\\[\n5 = 12 + b\n\\]\n\\[\nb = 5 - 12\n\\]\n\\[\nb = -7\n\\]\n\nTherefore, $a - b = 3 - (-7) = 3 + 7 = 10$.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{10}$.",
